<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<archimate:model xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:archimate="http://www.archimatetool.com/archimate" name="OMS Rust CAL Core Interfaces" id="m-oms-rust-cal-001" version="5.0.0">
  <folder name="Strategy" id="id-fb479a9b615e4ac8bd2e55cbf723ef92" type="strategy"/>
  <folder name="Business" id="id-60eb801611b14da89d6346eb18c91146" type="business"/>
  <folder name="Application" id="f-app" type="application">
    <folder name="Error Handling" id="f-err">
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="CalError" id="e-calerror">
        <documentation>Rust equivalent of UCIException. Primary error carrier for all fallible CAL operations. Implements std::error::Error plus Send plus Sync. Fields: kind (CalErrorKind), message (String), source (Option of boxed Error). CERTs: CAL-005204, CAL-005369, CAL-016043. Ref: Section 5.1.2.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="CalErrorKind" id="e-calerror-kind">
        <documentation>Non-exhaustive enum classifying CAL error conditions. Variants: InitializationFailure (CAL-005204), TopicUnavailable (CAL-005369), ResourcesUnavailable (CAL-016043), InvalidState (Table 5.9-2), UuidConformanceError (CAL-016477), OperationNotPermitted (CAL-016050), AsbFailed, InvalidServiceIdentifier, SerializationError, AbstractInstantiation (CAL-016035), ImplementationError.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationInterface" name="CalResult(T)" id="e-calresult">
        <documentation>Type alias: type CalResult(T) = Result(T, CalError). Return type for all fallible CAL operations. Replaces C++ and Java exception propagation. Every operation that can signal a UCIException in C++ returns CalResult(T) in the Rust CAL. Ref: Section 5.1.2.</documentation>
      </element>
    </folder>
    <folder name="UUID" id="f-uuid">
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="UUID" id="e-caluuid">
        <documentation>RFC 4122 conformant UUID enforced by construction. Newtype wrapper over uuid::Uuid. Validation applied at every construction path. Invariants: Variant = RFC 4122 Leach-Salz (CAL-016479), Version in {1, 3, 4} (CAL-005181). CERTs: CAL-016477, CAL-016479, CAL-005181.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="ServiceUuids" id="e-serviceuuids">
        <documentation>Aggregates UUIDs identifying a CAL Client service context. Fields: system (CalUuid), service (CalUuid), subsystem (Option of CalUuid), components (Vec of CalUuid), capabilities (Vec of CalUuid). Retrieved via AbstractServiceBus::uuids() after initialisation. CERT: CAL-005203.</documentation>
      </element>
    </folder>
    <folder name="Accessors" id="f-acc">
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationInterface" name="RequiredField(T)" id="e-reqfield">
        <documentation>Trait providing read/write access to a field that is always present (xs:element minOccurs=1 maxOccurs=1). Methods: get() returning reference to T, get_mut() returning mutable reference to T, set(value: T). Ref: Section 5.5.1.2, 5.5.4.2.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationInterface" name="OptionalField(T)" id="e-optfield">
        <documentation>Trait for optionally-populated fields. Created in DISABLED state (CAL-005254). Methods: is_enabled(), get() returning Option, set(value) which enables, disable(). CERTs: CAL-005254, CAL-005290, CAL-005293, CAL-005294, CAL-005296.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationInterface" name="BoundedListField(T)" id="e-bndfield">
        <documentation>Trait for bounded list of homogeneous elements. Created EMPTY (CAL-005264). Methods: len(), is_empty(), max_bound(), min_bound(), reserve(n), push(elem), pop(), clear(), get(i). CERT: CAL-005264.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationInterface" name="ChoiceField(V)" id="e-choicefield">
        <documentation>Trait for discriminated union field. Created UNINITIALIZED (CAL-005267). V is a generated enum with one variant per schema choice alternative. Methods: get(), get_mut(), set(value: V), clear(), is_set(). CERT: CAL-005267.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationInterface" name="CalMessage" id="e-calmessage">
        <documentation>Marker trait for top-level publishable OMS message types. Only CalMessage types may be associated with a topic. Non-abstract messages implement this trait. Abstract message types must not be instantiated (CAL-016035). CERTs: CAL-016033, CAL-016035.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationInterface" name="CalSubMessage" id="e-calsubmessage">
        <documentation>Marker trait for nested sub-message types used as fields within CalMessage types. CalSubMessage instances cannot be sent or received outside the context of an encapsulating CalMessage. Ref: Section 5.5.</documentation>
      </element>
    </folder>
    <folder name="Abstract Service Bus" id="f-asb">
      <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="CalInstanceConfig" id="e-calinstanceconfig">
        <documentation>Configuration parameters for initialising a CAL instance. Fields: service_identifier (String, CAL-005201), asb_identifier (String, CAL-005202), network_config_path (PathBuf, Section 4.7). CERTs: CAL-005201, CAL-005202.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="AsbConnectionState" id="e-asbstate">
        <documentation>Enum of ASB connection states per Table 5.9-1: Initializing (optional), Normal (required), Degraded (optional), Inoperable (optional), Failed (required). Provides validate_transition() enforcing the Figure 5.9-2 state machine rules.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="AsbStatus" id="e-asbstatus">
        <documentation>Snapshot of current ASB connection status delivered to registered listeners and returned by polling calls. Fields: state (AsbConnectionState), description (String). Ref: Section 5.9.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationInterface" name="AsbStatusListener" id="e-asblistener">
        <documentation>Trait implemented by CAL Clients to receive ASB connection status change notifications via callback. Method: on_status_change(status: AsbStatus). Called immediately upon registration (CAL-016366), then on every subsequent state change.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationInterface" name="AbstractServiceBus" id="e-asb">
        <documentation>Primary CAL instance interface (object-safe). Methods: service_id(), uuids() (CAL-005203), connection_status(), register_status_listener() (CAL-016366), unregister_status_listener(), close(). Generic factory methods (create_writer, create_reader) live in the non-object-safe extension trait AbstractServiceBusExt. CERTs: CAL-005201, CAL-005202, CAL-005203, CAL-016366.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationInterface" name="AbstractServiceBusExt(M)" id="e-asbext">
        <documentation>Non-object-safe extension trait of AbstractServiceBus providing generic factory methods for typed Writers and Readers. Bounded by M: CalMessage + Serialize + DeserializeOwned at the impl site. Methods: create_writer(topic: &amp;str, qos: TopicQos) returning CalResult(Box(dyn AbstractWriter(M))), create_reader(topic: &amp;str, qos: TopicQos) returning CalResult(Box(dyn AbstractReader(M))). CERTs: CAL-005364, CAL-005374.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationInterface" name="AbstractWriter(M)" id="e-writer">
        <documentation>Trait for a CAL Writer associated with exactly one Client Topic (CAL-005368). M is a CalMessage type. Methods: topic() returning &amp;str, write(message: &amp;M) returning CalResult(()) — errors on topic unavailable (CAL-005369) or resources unavailable (CAL-016043), close() consuming Box(Self). Accepts TopicQos at creation (CAL-005210). CERTs: CAL-005364, CAL-005368, CAL-005369, CAL-016043.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationInterface" name="AbstractReader(M)" id="e-reader">
        <documentation>Trait for a CAL Reader associated with exactly one Client Topic (CAL-005378). M is a CalMessage type. Callback interface (CAL-005379): add_listener, remove_listener. Polling interface (CAL-005380): read(timeout) blocking (CAL-016049), read_no_wait() non-blocking. read() returns OperationNotPermitted when listeners are registered (CAL-016050). Messages removed from buffer on delivery (CAL-016052) or after listener dispatch (CAL-016045). Topic connection established at creation (CAL-005394); buffering begins per QoS (CAL-016044). CERTs: CAL-005374, CAL-005378, CAL-005379, CAL-005380, CAL-005391, CAL-005392, CAL-005394, CAL-016044, CAL-016045, CAL-016049, CAL-016050, CAL-016052.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationInterface" name="MessageListener(M)" id="e-msglistener">
        <documentation>Callback trait registered with AbstractReader to receive incoming CAL Messages (CAL-005391). Method: on_message(msg: &amp;Arc(M)) — called once per received message with a shared reference (CAL-005392). The reference remains valid for the duration of the call (CAL-016046). CERTs: CAL-005391, CAL-005392, CAL-016046.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationFunction" name="CalInstanceFactory" id="e-calfactory">
        <documentation>Platform entry-point function for obtaining a fully initialised CAL instance. Signature: fn(config: CalInstanceConfig) returning CalResult of boxed AbstractServiceBus. CERTs: CAL-005201, CAL-005202.</documentation>
      </element>
    </folder>
    <folder name="QoS" id="f-qos">
      <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="TopicQos" id="e-topicqos">
        <documentation>QoS configuration aggregate accepted by create_writer and create_reader (CAL-005210). Contains four independent axes: MessageBuffer, Expiration, Reliability, TimeBasedFilter. Default: no buffer limit, no expiration, best-effort, no filter. CERT: CAL-005210.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="MessageBuffer" id="e-msgbuffer">
        <documentation>Limits buffered message count. Writer (CAL-005445): drop oldest when writer buffer full. Reader (CAL-016079): drop oldest when reader buffer full. Field: max_count: Option(usize) — None means unlimited. CERTs: CAL-005444, CAL-005445, CAL-016079.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="Expiration" id="e-expiration">
        <documentation>Time-to-live for Reader buffer messages. Expired messages are dropped before delivery (CAL-005437). Field: ttl: Option(Duration) — None means no expiration. CERT: CAL-005437.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="Reliability" id="e-reliability">
        <documentation>Delivery guarantee level. BestEffort: no retransmission. Reliable: resend undelivered messages while available (CAL-005434), preserving order (CAL-016076). CERTs: CAL-005434, CAL-016076.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="TimeBasedFilter" id="e-tbf">
        <documentation>Reader-side minimum inter-arrival filter. Messages received within min_separation of the last accepted message are dropped (CAL-005431). Field: min_separation: Option(Duration). CERT: CAL-005431.</documentation>
      </element>
    </folder>
    <folder name="ZMQ Implementation" id="f-zmq">
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="ZmqAsb" id="e-zmqasb">
        <documentation>omq-tokio RADIO/DISH-backed concrete implementation of AbstractServiceBus and AbstractServiceBusExt. Owns a RADIO socket via a background tokio task; ZmqWriters enqueue through a channel. Each ZmqReader owns an independent DISH socket in its own background task. Transport URI from CalConfig [[transport]]. For multi-process topologies, peer RADIO URIs are registered via add_receive_peer(); readers connect DISH to all peers. RADIO binds for TCP/inproc; RADIO connects for UDP (DISH binds for UDP). Serialization controlled by SerializationFormat in transport config.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="ZmqWriter(M)" id="e-zmqwriter">
        <documentation>Concrete AbstractWriter for the ZMQ transport. Serializes M to XML (compact or indented per SerializationFormat), assembles a two-part RADIO/DISH message [group=topic, payload=XML], and sends via the shared ZmqAsb write channel. Close is a no-op — channel is shared with ZmqAsb. CERTs realized: CAL-005368, CAL-005369, CAL-016043.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:ApplicationComponent" name="ZmqReader(M)" id="e-zmqreader">
        <documentation>Concrete AbstractReader for the ZMQ transport. Owns a DISH socket in a background tokio task that connects to registered peer RADIO URIs and joins the topic group. Dispatches to registered MessageListeners (callback mode) or buffers in a std::sync::mpsc channel (polling mode). Callback and polling modes are mutually exclusive (CAL-016050). Close aborts the background task. CERTs realized: CAL-005378, CAL-005379, CAL-005380, CAL-005391, CAL-005392, CAL-005394, CAL-016044, CAL-016045, CAL-016049, CAL-016050, CAL-016052.</documentation>
      </element>
      <element xsi:type="archimate:DataObject" name="SerializationFormat" id="e-serformat">
        <documentation>Enum controlling XML serialization style on a ZMQ transport. Variants: Xml (compact, no whitespace), PrettyXml (indented, human-readable). Configured per transport via the 'format' key in [[transport]] TOML. Default: Xml.</documentation>
      </element>
    </folder>
  </folder>
  <folder name="Technology" id="f-tech" type="technology">
    <element xsi:type="archimate:TechnologyService" name="ASB Network Service" id="e-asbtech">
      <documentation>Technology layer representation of the Abstract Service Bus network service. Realizes the messaging infrastructure used by AbstractServiceBus implementations. Ref: Section 4.12. This could be ActiveMQ, zfs, DDS, etc.</documentation>
    </element>
    <element xsi:type="archimate:Artifact" name="Network Configuration" id="e-netconfig">
      <documentation>Configuration artifact specifying valid CAL Topics, network connections, and transport layer mappings for a CAL instance. Ref: Section 4.7.</documentation>
    </element>
  </folder>
